/target/
*.log
.DS_Store
/crates/*/fuzz/target/
/crates/*/fuzz/corpus/
/crates/*/fuzz/artifacts/
# A Soli app's publisher key, generated on first serve; never committed.
**/config/eui_publisher.pkcs8
# a saved mail account: an address and an app password, never committed
**/config/account.json
# a local copy of a mailbox
**/config/messages.json
**/config/messages-*.json
**/config/accounts.json
# pictures fetched out of a mail: someone else's bytes, never committed
**/public/mail-img/
**/public/mail-att/
# A letter written out as a page, for the browser button. Someone else's
# correspondence, rendered: it belongs on the machine that fetched it.
**/public/mail-page/
**/tmp/eui-uploads/

# A Soli app's environment: never committed.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Album art fetched from a catalogue at runtime: a cache, never committed.
examples/demo-app/public/covers/
# Pictures fetched from x.com for the feed, cached as PNG the same way.
examples/demo-app/public/x/
# Faces fetched from a font service at boot, named by weight and kept as a
# cache: the same shape as the two above, and the reason is the same one
# over again — a file the server downloaded is not a file the repository
# wrote. It also keeps somebody else's licence out of this tree.
examples/demo-app/public/fonts/
# What the tracker's Play button mixes: generated, never committed.
examples/demo-app/public/tracker/
# What somebody attached in Atrium, and the thumbnails made from it. These
# are a *person's* files — a photograph off their phone, a document they
# dragged in — sitting in a directory the application writes to at runtime.
# Nothing here belongs in a repository, and the one thing worse than the
# megabytes is committing somebody's holiday snap by accident.
examples/demo-app/public/chat/
# Where an upload lands before the application decides to keep it (01 §6).
examples/demo-app/tmp/

# `scripts/make-icons.py` is imported as a module when its PNG decoder is
# wanted elsewhere, and Python leaves this behind when it is.
__pycache__/

# Where scripts/make-android-apk.sh leaves the package it built.
dist/

# The page's client, written by `cargo run -p xtask -- web`. Built in CI and
# rsynced with the site it serves; a multi-megabyte binary rebuilt on every
# client change does not belong in a history.
# `cargo run -p xtask -- web` writes these; the source is assets/web/.
www/public/eui/
doc/public/eui/
examples/demo-app/public/eui/

# A soli-proxy configuration that happens to sit at this root; it belongs to
# the machine that serves the examples, not to this repository.
/config.toml
# Touching this is what asks the proxy for a blue/green deploy. It is a
# gesture, not a file: its contents never matter and its mtime never means
# anything twice.
examples/demo-app/restart.txt
# What somebody attached through the demo's file pickers, and whatever the
# server wrote beside it. Same as public/chat/ above, and the same reason:
# these are a person's files, sitting in a directory the application writes.
examples/demo-app/public/files/
# The site's two faces, excluded for the reason demo-app's are: a file the
# application serves is not a file the repository wrote, and it keeps
# somebody else's licence out of this tree. `examples/eui-site/README.md`
# says which faces and where they go; without them the page draws in the
# client's own Inter and says so.
examples/eui-site/public/fonts/

# `clients/` holds the language bindings, each one its own repository —
# eui-ruby is the first. A repository inside a repository is nobody's
# submodule: it is cloned and pushed on its own, and this tree only ever
# has a copy of it sitting here.
/clients/

# Worktrees an agent made for itself. Each one is a clone of this
# repository, and a repository inside a repository is nobody's friend.
.claude/worktrees/
